    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0557" n="1235" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1235"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Romero</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 25, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have had the honor to receive your note
                    of the 23d instant, relative to an alleged forcible taking from the jurisdiction
                    of the Mexican tribunals, by Acting Rear-Admiral Wilkes, of the steamer
                    Noe-Daquy, captured by the authorities of Yucatan for being engaged in the slave
                    trade.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to acquaint you that a translation of your
                    communication will be at once submitted to the Secretary of the Navy, with a
                    request for an inquiry into the case, with a view to such further proceedings as
                    the result may be found to call for.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of the occasion, sir, to offer you a renewed assurance of my very
                    high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Señor Don <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matias Romero</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
